cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these datasets, the real-world benchmark, or the tooling, please cite this repository."
title: "Caliber Drift and Capability Boundaries: An Audit Protocol for Software-Verification Evaluation"
abstract: >-
  A reproducibility package for auditing the evaluator: a measurement-drift algebra (caliber signature,
  four drift types, seven axioms of which only two are independent), an identifiability/correctability/
  sample-complexity boundary analysis, a 1,147-sample x 8-asset frozen detection matrix with four-state
  verdicts (pass/fail/unknown/contradict), and a real-world benchmark of 110 reconstructed C++ defects
  with NVD-verified CVE provenance.
